Taxonomy and Layer 2 Configuration
This section outlines the domain-specific taxonomy used for the crop insurance purchase use case and defines the expected configurations.
Domain: The Beckn domain under which this flow operates is agri:uki, reserved for agricultural service transactions related to soil testing, agri-input planning, and allied diagnostics on the UKI Network.
Category: Soil testing services are classified under the category soil-testing, encompassing different types of soil sample analysis for agricultural planning purposes.
Item Tags:
collection-type — Specifies how the soil sample will be provided: either pickup from the farm (farm-pickup) or farmer-delivered to testing centre (centre-dropoff).
test-types — List of soil tests requested, such as NPK, pH, OC, EC, Zn, B, Cu, Fe, Mo, Mn, Soil Texture, Soil Moisture, Contaminants, CEC.
report-format — Specifies in what format the soil test report will be delivered to the user (e.g., PDF, Video, Image).
Fulfillment Type:  Soil sample pickup and test report delivery are treated as fulfillments. Pickup involves agent arrival at farm (PickUp), or farmer drop-off to the service center (DropOff). Final soil reports are delivered digitally via documents (no physical goods involved at the delivery stage).
Payment Method:  ON-FULFILLMENT — Payment is collected at the point of service execution (sample pickup or drop-off), typically in cash mode.
Enumerations and Mandatory Fields:
Farm location details (GPS coordinates and address) must be mandatorily provided in fulfillment.start.location.
Collection type (farm-pickup or centre-dropoff) must be specified as item-level tags.
Test types selected by the farmer must be listed explicitly under item.tags.
Final soil test report delivery must include a document link (documents) at fulfillment completion.
Payment collection must correctly specify the collected_by and payment_collection_mode parameters.


